"""Shared footer policy for all staff, markets and Meta creative formats."""

FOOTER_VERSION = "SPORTS CAVE COMPACT RESTORED SUBHEADLINE FOOTER V2"
COMPACT_FOOTER_RULES = f'{FOOTER_VERSION}\nApply to every Sports Cave black footer in every ad format and staff account.\nKeep existing layouts that have no black footer; do not add a footer to them.\nEvery Sports Cave ad that uses a black footer must show exactly three centred lines in this order:\n1. The assigned approved headline, preserving its wording and case.\n2. The exact FOMO supporting sentence assigned to this ad, directly below the headline on one line.\n3. CLAIM YOUR EDITION in plain antique-gold lettering.\nCopy the resolved headline, FOMO sentence and CTA verbatim into each individual image-generation prompt. Preserve saved assignments. If the brief calls for automatic selection, resolve it using the existing approved selection rules before generation. Keep 100 in antique gold with no underline.\nFooter asset and Collector Series plaque\nUse sports-cave-ad-footer-example.jpg from the Assets folder as the approved footer artwork. In ChatGPT, use the project source with that exact filename and attach the actual image as a separate reference alongside the product image for each applicable black-footer cover. Where the Companion can composite the footer, place the asset directly and typeset the copy over it.\nKeep the footer full-width, opaque and flush to the bottom, with the fixed footer geometry below. Preserve the satin folds and the single muted charcoal Collector Series plaque with its scalloped rim. Apply the seam shimmer specified below. Match the plaque’s relative size and right-side position in the asset. Preserve its SC monogram, stars, laurel and ring lettering. The footer asset already contains the plaque. Keep the original product reference separate from this footer treatment.\nSports Cave antique-gold shimmer at the photo–footer seam\nFor a 1024 × 1024 square, the photo occupies the top 815 px and the footer occupies the bottom 209 px, starting at y = 815 from the top. This is the fixed geometry for all square black-footer ads. Scale this split proportionally for other square resolutions. For non-square layouts keep the existing format-specific split. Use exactly one uninterrupted full-width, thin antique-gold line at the existing seam, flush with the topmost edge of the black footer where it directly touches the photo. Place the shimmer on the first row of the footer, within the original border thickness and inside the 209 px. The shimmer is included in the footer height. Reserve zero extra vertical space for this treatment: no inset, gap, extra strip, second line, or movement of the seam or copy.\nUse the supplied Sports Cave gold streak as the finish reference: soft dark-gold tails and a narrow, restrained brighter gold glint tapering horizontally into the antique-gold base. Confine all shimmer to the line itself, with no vertical glow. In a still, show a frozen glint. Where animation is already supported, the glint may travel along that same fixed line. Keep the line continuous and free of any logo, monogram, diamond, icon or lettering.\nKeep 100 gold wherever the approved headline calls for it. Use no underline or ornament below 100 or elsewhere beneath the headline. The scalloped Collector Series plaque belongs in its existing right-hand position within the footer. If compositing, recolour or replace only the baked-in border pixels at the seam. For direct compositing at 1024 × 1024, use sports-cave-ad-footer-example.jpg at its native 1024 × 209 size, anchored to y = 815. Check the final dimensions and seam position before export.\nAdd exactly the three existing lines in order: the ad’s assigned headline, its exact FOMO supporting sentence, and CLAIM YOUR EDITION in plain antique-gold lettering. Preserve the existing typography, gold 100 treatment and wording. Centre each of the headline, FOMO line and CTA on the full canvas midpoint, x = 512 at 1024 px wide. The plaque is a background detail. Allow the foreground copy to sit over it if needed, with clean contrast and the same centre axis for all three lines. Use compact, balanced spacing and check readability at mobile size. If the exact image asset is unavailable, flag it so the trial is not reported as an asset match.\nPreserve the headline wording, font, size, colours, gold highlights and alignment. Keep the gold 100 unadorned. Do not rewrite, shorten or standardise headline variations, or move the supporting sentence into the headline.\nRestore the exact saved supporting sentence and historical selection rules; never invent replacement wording. Set it in Montserrat Regular, 24–26 px at 1024 px, softer warm off-white, centred on one line. Keep it secondary; no blank row or spacer.\nKeep CLAIM YOUR EDITION exactly unchanged, including its existing gold colour, typography, tracking and styling.\nKeep the full-width opaque matte-black panel flush to the bottom, with the Sports Cave divider specified in the footer rules along the top. No fade, gradient, transparency or floating overlay.\nUse the fixed 815 px photo and 209 px footer split at 1024 × 1024. Retain the 42–48 px headline, 26–28 px CTA and 64–72 px horizontal safe margins. Fit the three lines vertically with compact gaps and balanced top and bottom breathing room. Keep every line clear of the panel edges. Fit the type and spacing inside the fixed panel. Scale typography and safe areas proportionally for other square resolutions.\nThe framed edition remains the dominant visual. Preserve all artwork, frame, room, brand-colour, realism and generation-workflow instructions. Restoring the supporting sentence must not add a scarcity claim or alter any product detail.\nInspect the final image: exact headline, assigned supporting sentence and CTA, unchanged compact balanced footer, preserved separator and branding, dominant complete framed edition. Report unresolved defects honestly.'


def apply_footer_contract(prompt):
    """Include the shared policy once at the public prompt boundary."""
    if COMPACT_FOOTER_RULES in prompt:
        return prompt
    return COMPACT_FOOTER_RULES + "\n\n" + prompt
